usage: plan.py commit [-h] [--plans-root PLANS_ROOT] --role
                      {executor,reviewer,fix} [--type TYPE] [--scope SCOPE]
                      [--summary SUMMARY] [--trailer KEY: VALUE] [--path PATH]
                      [--leave-outside] [--dry-run] [--actor ACTOR] [--json]
                      plan ref

create one scoped Git commit for an item or unit operation

positional arguments:
  plan                  plan id, PLAN<N> or path
  ref                   local Pn.m or Pn.m/U#

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --plans-root PLANS_ROOT
                        plans/ directory (default: nearest up from cwd)
  --role {executor,reviewer,fix}
  --type TYPE           Conventional Commit type (default: feat, docs or fix
                        by role)
  --scope SCOPE         commit scope (default: settings.commit.scope or plan
                        codename)
  --summary SUMMARY     commit subject (default: item or unit title)
  --trailer KEY: VALUE
  --path PATH           explicit extra ownership path
  --leave-outside       leave foreign dirty paths untouched
  --dry-run             show selection and message without writing
  --actor ACTOR         PROVIDER/MODEL[/EFFORT] (default: the item executor,
                        else plan authoring)
  --json
